odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37823:The fo:margin-left attribute is usable with the following elements: <style:graphic-properties> 17.21, <style:header-footer-properties> 17.5, <style:page-layout-properties> 17.2, <style:paragraph-properties> 17.6, <style:section-properties> 17.11 and <style:table-properties> 17.15.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37825:The values of the fo:margin-left attribute are a value of type length 18.3.19 or a value of type percent 18.3.24.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37999:If the text:list-level-position-and-space-mode attribute on the same <style:list-level-properties> element has the value label-alignment, the value of the text:min-label-width attribute is treated as 0 and the fo:text-align attribute specifies the horizontal alignment of the list label at the alignment position. The alignment position is specified by the fo:margin-left 20.207 and fo:text-indent 20.225 attributes of its child element <style:list-level-label-alignment> 17.20.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38539:20.254 style:column-width
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38541:The style:column-width attribute specifies a fixed width for a column.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38543:The style:column-width attribute is usable with the following element: <style:table-column-properties> 17.16.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38545:The style:column-width attribute has the data type positiveLength 18.3.27.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39383:5)Values of the fo:margin-left 20.207 attribute, which can also be given by the fo:margin, and fo:text-indent 19.246 attributes, that meet one of these conditions: 
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39386:2.Values of the fo:margin-left attributes are the same and values of the fo:text-indent attributes are non-negative. 
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39388:3.Value of the fo:margin-left attribute of one paragraph whose value of the fo:text-indent attribute is non-negative is the same as the sum of values of the fo:margin-left and fo:text-indent attributes of the other paragraph whose value of the fo:text-indent attribute is negative. 
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39390:4.Both values of the fo:text-indent attributes are negative and the sums of values of the fo:margin-left and fo:text-indent attributes are equal. 
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41753:•false: paragraph style determines position of tab stops relative to the outer edge of the margin that is specified by fo:margin or fo:margin-left of the paragraph. 
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41755:•true: paragraph style determines the position of tab stops relative to the inner edge of the margin that is specified by fo:margin or fo:margin-left of the paragraph. Exception: the tab stop set by applied list style is determined by the paragraph style relative to the outer edge of the margin that is specified by fo:margin or fo:margin-left of the paragraph. 
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41759:Note: In right-to-left layout environments, the paragraph's right margin is specified by fo:margin-left, and its tab stop positions are relative to the right edge.

